            <ArticleTitle>Radiotherapy for bone metastases of hepatocellular carcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Radiotherapeutic effects of 42 bone metastases in 26 hepatocellular carcinoma patients were retrospectively analyzed. Pain relief was observed in 79% of 37 bone metastases treated (29/37). Antitumor effects and improvement of paralysis were also observed in 88% (8/9) and 17% (1/6), respectively. The toxicities experienced were tolerable. Radiotherapy was an effective means of palliation in the treatment of hepatocellular carcinoma bone metastases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
